# LogQL quick reference
[group('doc'), no-exit-message]
cheatsheet:
    #!/usr/bin/env -S colored-md

    # LOGQL QUICK REFERENCE

    ## STREAM SELECTORS (the required starting point of every LogQL query)

    ```
    {label="v"}              exact-match filter
        # every stream where service_name="api" (all LogQL queries start with a {})
        {service_name="api"}

    {label!="v"}             not-equal
        # every api-service stream except from job=prometheus
        {service_name="api", job!="prometheus"}

    {label=~"re"}            regex match (RE2 syntax)
        # streams from any api-* service
        {service_name=~"api.*"}

    {label!~"re"}            regex not-match
        # everything NOT from probe.*
        {service_name!~"probe.*"}

    {a="1", b="2"}           multiple label matchers - AND (commas are never OR)
        # both labels must match on the same stream
        {service_name="api", k8s_container_name="app"}

    NOTE: regex label matchers (`=~`, `!~`) are FULLY ANCHORED. `=~"api"` is `=~"^api$"`.
          Use `.*` on both ends for substring (`=~".*api.*"`), or `=~"api.*"` for prefix.
          (Line filters below are the OPPOSITE - see the note in that section.)
    ```

    ## LINE FILTERS (content of raw log line, applied BEFORE parsing - fast)

    ```
    |= "text"                line contains substring
        # any line mentioning feature-flags anywhere
        {service_name="api"} |= "feature-flags"

    != "text"                line does not contain substring
        # exclude noisy health checks
        {service_name="api"} != "/healthz"

    |~ "regex"               line matches regex (RE2)
        # 5xx status codes anywhere in the line
        {service_name="api"} |~ "status=5[0-9]{2}"

    !~ "regex"               line does not match regex
        # exclude both healthz and readyz probes
        {service_name="api"} !~ "GET /(healthz|readyz)"

    (?i) inline flag         case-insensitive within a regex (use inside `|~`/`!~`)
        # match "error"/"ERROR"/"Error"
        {service_name="api"} |~ "(?i)error"

    |= ip("cidr")            CIDR match (Loki extension)
        # log lines whose text contains an IP in the given CIDR
        {service_name="proxy"} |= ip("10.0.0.0/8")

    NOTE: line filter regexes (`|~`, `!~`) are RE2 SEARCH - NOT anchored (opposite of label matchers).
          `|~ "error"` matches any line containing "error" anywhere; use `^`/`$` yourself if you need anchoring.
    ```

    ## LABEL FILTERS (act on labels AFTER parsing - slower than line filters)

    ```
    | label="v"              filter on a parsed/existing label
        # `level` becomes a label after `| json`, then filter to ERROR
        {service_name="api"} | json | level="ERROR"

    | n > NUM                numeric comparison (label auto-coerced)
        # slow requests, > 100 ms
        {service_name="api"} | json | duration_ms > 100

    | dur > 500ms            duration comparison (LogQL types: 100us, 5s, 2m, 1h, ...)
        # requests slower than half a second
        {service_name="api"} | logfmt | duration > 500ms

    chained filters          each `|` filter is AND; read left-to-right
        # errors AND slow AND from a specific pod
        {service_name="api"} | json | level="ERROR" | duration_ms > 100 | pod="api-7f8"

    NOTE: regex label filters (`| foo=~"..."`) are FULLY ANCHORED, same as stream selectors.
          Wrap with `.*` for substring; line filters (`|~`) remain the unanchored exception.
    ```

    ## PARSERS (turn line content into structured labels)

    ```
    | json                   parse JSON body; all top-level fields become labels
        # after this you can filter on .level, .msg, .duration_ms, etc.
        {service_name="api"} | json

    | json name="path"       extract one nested field into a named label (dot path)
        # copy request.duration_ms into label `dur`
        {service_name="api"} | json dur="request.duration_ms"

    | logfmt                 parse key=value logfmt; each key becomes a label
        # for lines like `level=info duration=42ms msg="ok"`
        {service_name="api"} | logfmt

    | regexp "re"            regex with (?P<name>...) named captures -> labels
        # capture method and path from a request line
        {service_name="api"} | regexp "(?P<method>[A-Z]+) (?P<path>/[^ ]+)"

    | pattern "<a> <b> <c>"  simpler than regexp - space-delimited placeholders -> labels
        # split "GET /api 200 42ms" into method/path/status/dur
        {service_name="api"} | pattern "<method> <path> <status> <dur>"

    | unpack                 unpack Promtail's packed labels (from the `pack` stage)
        {service_name="api"} | unpack
    ```

    ## LINE / LABEL FORMAT (reshape output after parsing)

    ```
    | line_format "tmpl"     rewrite the log line using Go text/template with labels
        # replace verbose line with compact "<level> <msg>"
        {service_name="api"} | json | line_format "{{'{{.level}} {{.msg}}'}}"

    | label_format new=old   rename / synthesize labels via templates
        # add a `slug` label = "<service>-<pod>"
        {service_name="api"} | label_format slug="{{'{{.service_name}}-{{.pod}}'}}"
    ```

    ## METRIC QUERIES (turn matching lines into a time series)

    ```
    rate({..}[5m])           per-second event rate over the 5m window
        # events per second on this stream
        rate({service_name="api"}[5m])

    count_over_time({..}[5m])  total number of matching lines in the window
        # error count in the last 5m
        count_over_time({service_name="api"} |= "ERROR" [5m])

    bytes_over_time({..}[5m])  total bytes ingested in the window
        # ingest volume per stream over 5m
        bytes_over_time({service_name="api"}[5m])

    sum by (label) (...)     group by label (same shape as PromQL)
        # error rate per pod
        sum by (pod) (rate({service_name="api"} |= "ERROR" [5m]))

    topk / bottomk           top or bottom N series
        # 3 loudest pods by log rate
        topk(3, sum by (pod) (rate({service_name="api"}[5m])))
    ```

    ## COMMON PATTERNS

    ```
    # error rate: what fraction of lines are errors in the last 5m?
    sum(count_over_time({service_name="api"} |= "ERROR" [5m]))
      / sum(count_over_time({service_name="api"} [5m]))

    # top 5 chattiest pods
    topk(5, sum by (pod) (rate({service_name="api"}[5m])))

    # count occurrences of a specific event over an hour
    count_over_time({service_name="api"} |= "user login" [1h])

    # extract a numeric field and filter on it (parsed after `| json`)
    {service_name="api"} | json | user_id="42"

    # ingest bytes-per-second per service
    sum by (service_name) (rate({service_name=~".+"}[5m]))
    ```

    ## SEE ALSO

    - `loki doc` for the full list of LogQL / Loki doc links.

